Z||000000||glava2876||12-24-2001||09:54 PM||||I have two questions, actually more, but just two now.1)I replaced the alternator belt on the duke durring the summer. It kept sqeeking periodically, so i'd tighten it a little. Long story short, it started throwwing the belt an then the belt broke. What could be causing this? 2)My car overheated the other day when I let it run for over twenty minutes, I couldn't shut it down since the alt belt broke, but AC was still turning water pump. It seems as though the fan only runs if I run the AC.I replaced the original sender for the temperature gauge and the gauge still won't work -is there a relation ship between the fan operation and the temperature sending unit? I still have a couple of disconnected wires on the bell housing side near the fire wall -maybe these are related? Thanks, Glen  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||johnt671||12-25-2001||10:38 AM||||There is a fan switch on the firewall side of the head that has two wires running to it with A/C.  It's hard to see it, but if you go down from the sending unit for the temp guage, you can barely see it.  Mine was hard to spot because it had melted.  This controls the fan.  I put a manual switch on mine. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||glava2876||12-25-2001||01:24 PM||||John thanks, that sounds like what may have happened -I'll try a test by powering the melted wires. Happy Holidays, Glen||||reg||6
Z||000003||ITB 2M4||12-25-2001||02:34 PM||||There's a pretty good chance your water pump has been replaced at some point.  And the just about the only way you can find one now is without the water pump pulley on it already.  So you have to take the old pulley off, and put it on the new pump.  If the pulley is not installed to the right 'depth' on the pump shaft, it creates a mis-alignment for the belt.  I had the battery slide over in my race car and hit the pulley just enough to start the belt to squeaking every time I started it up.  Eventually, it started throwing the belt.<P>As to the overheating, there could be several reasons.  Make sure that the water pump is still in good shape from throwing the belt.  Also, if you only have the belt going to the A/C compressor, the compressor has a clutch system in it, but I'm not sure how that would affect the water pump, just something to think about...<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4<BR>AOL IM- DGPFiero||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||12-25-2001||02:42 PM||||Hey Glen!<BR>Remove your alternator and look at the bottom mount hole...<BR>Chances are, it is worn oblong, and allows the alternator to cant...<BR>I have replaced many alternators on the 2.5L that have done this, 3 on my own Fieros...<BR>Oh ya, when you reinstall the alt, be sure to get the bottom bolt TIGHT to prevent the alt from moving around and wearing out the mount hole...<P>If you want to continue using the A/C, that is fine, but if you remove it, look for a double grove alt pulley, so you can run dual belts to the alt...<BR>That way, it squeels much less!<BR>As to your overheating, Fieros do NOT like to idle for too long...<BR>But check your fan switch on the cylinder head to be sure it works...<P><BR>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">          <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Fierowrecker (edited 12-25-2001).]||||reg||1
